    "body": "- [YES] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [ YES] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\nThis pull request fixes 2 trivial vimdoc format issues as below:\r\n\r\n (doc) Fix format of vimdoc for LOCAL ADDITIONS use\r\n    \r\n    In order for nvim to list entries under \"LOCAL ADDITIONS:\", vimdoc\r\n    should start with particular format.\r\n     * The leading line should contain module name.\r\n     * There should be no leading space in it.\r\n    \r\n    I understand these documentation links under \"LOCAL ADDITION:\" for many\r\n    other packages are also missing under the modern delayed loading\r\n    situation under lazy.nvim. This makes it easy for many users to overlook\r\n    this kind of bug. Such issue of missing documentation links can be\r\n    addressed by, e.g.,  creating symlinks from ~/.config/nvim/doc/\r\n    directory. But this vimdoc format issuees of mini* were preventing to\r\n    list links for these documents while many other packages from other\r\n    author didn't suffer such issue since they followed this initial line\r\n    format convention.\r\n    \r\n    I (or nvim auto-formatter) also fixed missing newline at the\r\n    end-of-file.  This is generally good practice for text files.\r\n\r\n (doc) fix format for mini.txt for conceal\r\n    \r\n    In order for the conceal feature of nvim to work nicely, there should be\r\n    a space before leading \"|\" (bar) character. (I suppose this is dictated\r\n    by some treesitter logic used for this feature.)\r\n    \r\n    I also fixed one line with 2 leading spaces to match other lines.\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2023-03-13T14:20:44Z",
