            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thank you for the PR!\r\n\r\nI would be better if you opened issue to discuss this. The problem is that all documentation is auto-generated using 'mini.doc' module. I am currently looking for the best way to manage that first line for local additions.\r\n\r\nModeline (last line of help files) seems to be formatted in the same way as Neovim's built-in help files are. So I don't thing it should be changed.\r\n\r\nAdding space is a good catch, thanks! I personally don't yet use tree-sitter for help files, so didn't see that.",
